      <fo:flow flow-name="xsl-region-body" start-indent="1in" end-indent="0pt">
         <fo:block id="service.jndi">
            <fo:block font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
               <fo:block margin-left="0pt">
                  <fo:block font-size="24.8832pt" font-weight="bold">
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                               space-before.optimum="0in"
                               space-before.minimum="0in"
                               space-before.maximum="0in"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               text-align="start"
                               start-indent="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                               font-size="28pt"
                               line-height="35pt"
                               font-weight="normal"
                               space-after="24pt">
                        <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                       provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                           <fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                 <fo:block>126</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-label>
                              <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                 <fo:block>JNDI Services Specification</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-body>
                           </fo:list-item>
                        </fo:list-block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               font-family="ProductusOSGiBookcItalic"
                               font-size="18pt"
                               line-height="25pt">
                        <fo:basic-link internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi">
                           <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                      font-family="inherit"
                                      letter-spacing="inherit"
                                      hyphenate="inherit">Version 1.0</fo:inline>
                        </fo:basic-link>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d95e87">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Introduction</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.1</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Introduction</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Naming and directory services have long been useful tools in the
    building of software systems. The ability to use a programming interface
    to publish and consume objects can provide many benefits to any system.
    The Java Naming and Directory Interface (JNDI) is a registry technology in
    Java applications, both in the Java SE and Java EE space. JNDI provides a
    vendor-neutral set of APIs that allow clients to interact with a naming
    service from different vendors.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI as used in the Java SE environment relies on the class
    loading model provided by the JDK to find providers. By default, it
    attempts to load the JNDI provider class using the Thread Context Class
    Loader. In an OSGi environment, this type of Context creation is not
    desirable since it relies on the JNDI provider classes being visible to
    the JNDI client, or require it to set the Context Class Loader; in both
    cases breaking modularity. For modularity reasons, it is important that
    clients are not required to express a dependency on the implementation of
    services they use.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This specification will define how JNDI can be utilized from within
    an OSGi framework. The specification consists of three key parts:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d95e92">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e93">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">OSGi Service Model</fo:inline> - How clients interact
        with JNDI when running inside an OSGi Framework.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e97">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Provider Model</fo:inline> - How JNDI providers
        can advertise their existence so they are available to OSGi and
        traditional clients.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e101">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-style="italic">Traditional Model</fo:inline> - How traditional JNDI
        applications and providers can continue to work in an OSGi Framework
        without needing to be rewritten when certain precautions are
        taken.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block id="d95e105">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.1.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Essentials</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e107">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e108">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Naming Service</fo:inline> - Provide an integration
          model for JNDI API clients and providers.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e112">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Flexible</fo:inline> - Provide a standard mechanism
          for publishing and locating JNDI providers.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e116">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Compatibility</fo:inline> - Support the traditional
          JNDI programming model used by Java SE and Java EE clients.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e120">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Service Based</fo:inline> - Provide a service model
          that clients and providers can use to leverage JNDI
          facilities.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e124">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Migration</fo:inline> - Provide a mechanism to access
          OSGi services from a JNDI context.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e128">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.1.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Entities</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e130">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e131">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Implementation</fo:inline> - The Implementer of
          the JNDI Context Manager, JNDI Provider Admin, and setter of the
          JNDI static singletons.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e135">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Client</fo:inline> - Any code running within an
          OSGi bundle that needs to use JNDI.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e139">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Context Manager </fo:inline> - A service that
          allows clients to obtain Contexts via a service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e143">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Provider Admin</fo:inline> - A service that
          allows the conversion of objects for providers.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e147">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Provider</fo:inline> - Provides a Context
          implementation.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e151">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Context</fo:inline> - A Context abstracts a
          namespace. Implementations are provided by JNDI providers and the
          Contexts are used by JNDI clients. The corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.Context</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e157">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Dir Context</fo:inline> - A sub-type of
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> that provides mechanisms for examining and
          updating the attributes of an object in a directory structure, and
          for performing searches in an hierarchical naming systems like LDAP.
          The corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.directory.DirContext</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e165">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Initial Context Factory</fo:inline> - A factory for
          creating instances of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects. This factory is
          used to integrate new JNDI Providers. In general, a single Initial
          Context Factory constructs <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects for a single
          provider implementation. The corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.spi.InitialContextFactory</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e175">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Initial Context Factory Builder</fo:inline> - A
          factory for <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> objects. A single
          Initial Context Factory Builder can construct
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> objects for different types of
          Contexts. The interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.spi.InitialContextFactoryBuilder</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e185">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object Factory</fo:inline> - Used in conversion of
          objects. The corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.spi.ObjectFactory</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e191">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Dir Object Factory</fo:inline> - An Object Factory
          that takes attribute information for object conversion. The
          corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.spi.DirObjectFactory</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e198">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object Factory Builder</fo:inline> - A factory for
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects. A single Object Factory Builder
          can construct <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> instances for different
          types of conversions. The corresponding interface is
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">javax.naming.spi.ObjectFactoryBuilder</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e208">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Reference</fo:inline> - A description of an object
          that can be turned into an object through an Object Factory. The
          associated <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Referenceable</fo:inline> interface implemented on an
          object indicates that it can provide a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline>
          object.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block start-indent="0pt">
                  <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                            space-before.optimum="1em"
                            space-before.maximum="2em"
                            space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                            space-after.optimum="1em"
                            space-after.maximum="2em"
                            keep-together.within-column="always"
                            id="d95e216">
                     <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                               xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                               space-before.optimum="5pt"
                               space-before.minimum="5pt"
                               space-before.maximum="5pt"
                               font-weight="normal"
                               font-size="9pt"
                               hyphenate="false"
                               space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                               space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                               space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                               start-indent="0pt"
                               font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                               font-style="italic"
                               keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                       provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                           <fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                 <fo:block>Figure 126.1</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-label>
                              <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                 <fo:block>JNDI Service Specification Service Entities</fo:block>
                              </fo:list-item-body>
                           </fo:list-item>
                        </fo:list-block>
                     </fo:block>
                     <fo:block id="d95e218" text-align="center">
                        <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.jndi/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.jndi/src/main/resources/spec/jndi-classes.svg)"
                                             width="auto"
                                             height="auto"
                                             content-width="7.000in"
                                             content-height="3.477in"
                                             text-align="center"/>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e221">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.1.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Dependencies</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The classes and interfaces used in this specification come from
      the following packages:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e224">javax.naming
javax.naming.spi
javax.naming.directory</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">These packages have no associated version. It is assumed they come
      from the runtime environment. This specification is based on Java SE 1.4
      or later.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e226">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.1.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Synopsis</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A client bundle wishing to make use of JNDI in order to access
      JNDI Providers such as LDAP or DNS in OSGi should not use the Naming
      Manager but instead use the JNDI Context Manager service. This service
      can be asked for a Context based on environment properties. The
      environment properties are based on an optional argument in the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">newInitialContext</fo:inline> method, the Java System properties, and
      an optional resource in the caller's bundle.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">These environment properties can specify an implementation class
      name for a factory that can create a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object. If
      such a class name is specified, then it is searched for in the service
      registry. If such a service is found, then that service is used to
      create a new Context, which is subsequently returned. If no class name
      is specified, the service registry is searched for Initial Context
      Factory services. These services are tried in ranking order, as
      specified in <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference.compareTo</fo:inline>, to see if they can
      create an appropriate Context, the first one that can create a Context
      is then used.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If no class name is specified, all Initial Context Factory Builder
      services are tried to see if they can create a Context, the first
      non-<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> result is used. If no Context can be found, a No
      Initial Context Exception is thrown. Otherwise, the JNDI Context Manager
      service returns an initial Context that uses the just created Context
      from a provider as the backing service. This initial Context delegates
      all operations to this backing Context, except operations that use a
      name that can be interpreted as a URL, that is, the name contains a
      colon. URL operations are delegated a URL Context that is associated
      with the used scheme. URL Contexts are found through the general object
      conversion facility provided by the JNDI Provider Admin service.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Provider Admin service provides a general object
      conversion facility that can be extended with Object Factory and Object
      Factory Builder services that are traditionally provided through the
      Naming Manager <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method. A specific case
      for this conversion is the use of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> objects.
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> objects can be used to store objects persistently
      in a Context implementation. Reference objects must be converted to
      their corresponding object when retrieved from a Context.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">During the client's use of a Context it is possible that its
      provider's service is unregistered. In this case the JNDI Context
      Manager must release the backing Context. If the initial Context is used
      and no backing Context is available, the JNDI Context Manager must
      re-create a new Context, if possible. Otherwise a Naming Exception is
      thrown. If subsequently a proper new backing Context can be created, the
      initial Context must start operating again.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Context Manager service must track the life cycle of a
      calling bundle and ensure that any returned <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects
      are closed and returned objects are properly cleaned up when the bundle
      is closed or the JNDI Context Manager service is unget.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When the client bundle is stopped, any returned initial Context
      objects are closed and discarded. If the Initial Context Factory, or
      Initial Context Factory Builder, service that created the initial
      Context goes away then the JNDI Context Manager service releases the
      Context backing the initial Context and attempts to create a replacement
      Context.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Clients and JNDI Context providers that are unaware of OSGi use
      static methods to connect to the JRE JNDI implementation. The
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class provides access to a Context from a
      provider and providers use the static <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> methods
      to do object conversion and find URL Contexts. This traditional model is
      not aware of OSGi and can therefore only be used reliably if the
      consequences of this lack of OSGi awareness are managed.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i3095960">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">JNDI Overview</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.2</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>JNDI Overview</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The Java Naming and Directory Interface (JNDI) provides an
    abstraction for namespaces that is included in Java SE. This section
    describes the basic concepts of JNDI as provided in Java SE. These
    concepts are later used in the service model provided by this
    specification.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e265">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Context and Dir Context</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-style="italic">
                     <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                    xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                    internal-destination="i3131859">
                        <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                   font-family="inherit"
                                   letter-spacing="inherit"
                                   hyphenate="inherit">[1] <fo:inline font-style="italic">Java Naming and Directory Interface</fo:inline>
                        </fo:inline>
                     </fo:basic-link>
                  </fo:inline> (JNDI) defines
      an API for <fo:inline font-style="italic">namespaces</fo:inline>. These namespaces are
      abstracted with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface. Namespaces that
      support <fo:inline font-style="italic">attributes</fo:inline>, such as a namespace as the
      Lightweight Directory Access Protocol (LDAP), are represented by the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">DirContext</fo:inline> class, which extends the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline>
      class. If applicable, a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object can be cast to a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">DirContext</fo:inline> object. The distinction is not relevant for this
      specification, except in places where it is especially mentioned.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface models a set of name-to-object
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">bindings</fo:inline> within a namespace. These bindings can be
      looked-up, created, and updated through the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline>
      interface. The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface can be used for federated,
      flat, or hierarchical namespaces.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e297">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Initial Context</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Obtaining a Context for a specific namespace, for example DNS, is
      handled through the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class. Creating an
      instance of this class will cause the JRE to find a
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">backing</fo:inline> Context. The Initial Context is only a
      facade for the backing Context. The facade context provides URL based
      lookups.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The backing Context is created by a <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI
      Provider</fo:inline>. How this backing Context is created is an elaborate
      process using class loading techniques or a provisioning mechanism
      involving <fo:inline font-style="italic">builders</fo:inline>, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3082552">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Naming Manager Singletons</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3082552"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>
      for more information about the builder provisioning mechanism.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If there is no Initial Context Factory Builder set, the class name
      of a class implementing the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> interface
      is specified as a property in the <fo:inline font-style="italic">environment</fo:inline>. The
      environment is a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Hashtable</fo:inline> object that is constructed from
      different sources and then merged with System properties and a resource
      in the calling bundle, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3083484">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Environment</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3083484"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. In a standard
      Java SE JNDI, the given class name is then used to construct an
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> object and this object is then used
      to create the backing Context. This process is depicted in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3118331">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">Figure 126.2 on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3118331"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.5em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="2em"
                         keep-together.within-column="always"
                         id="i3118331">
                  <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                            xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                            space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt"
                            font-weight="normal"
                            font-size="9pt"
                            hyphenate="false"
                            space-after.minimum="0.4em"
                            space-after.optimum="0.6em"
                            space-after.maximum="0.8em"
                            start-indent="0pt"
                            font-family="Proforma-Book,ArialUnicodeMS"
                            font-style="italic"
                            keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                     <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                    provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                        <fo:list-item>
                           <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                              <fo:block>Figure 126.2</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-label>
                           <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                              <fo:block>Backing Context</fo:block>
                           </fo:list-item-body>
                        </fo:list-item>
                     </fo:list-block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block id="d95e330" text-align="center">
                     <fo:external-graphic src="url(file:///home/stbischof/git/OSGI_MIGRATE/osgi_target/org.osgi.service.jndi/spec/org.osgi.spec.service.jndi/src/main/resources/spec/initial-backing-context.svg)"
                                          width="auto"
                                          height="auto"
                                          content-width="6.237in"
                                          content-height="1.427in"
                                          text-align="center"/>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e333">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>URL Context Factory</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class implements the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface. It can therefore delegate all the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface methods to the backing
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object. However, it provides a special URL lookup
      behavior for names that are formed like URLs, that is, names that
      contain a colon (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">':' \u003A</fo:inline>) character. This behavior is
      called a <fo:inline font-style="italic">URL lookup</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">URL lookups are not delegated to the backing Context but are
      instead first tried via a <fo:inline font-style="italic">URL Context</fo:inline> based lookup
      on the given scheme, like:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e354">myscheme:foo</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">For example a lookup using
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">acme:foo/javax.sql.DataSource</fo:inline> results in a URL Context
      being used, rather than the backing Context.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">JNDI uses class loading techniques to search for an
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> class that can be used to create this URL
      Context. The Naming Manager provides a static method
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getURLContext</fo:inline> for this purpose. If such a URL Context is
      found, it is used with the requested operation and uses the full URL. If
      no such URL Context can be found, the backing Context is asked to
      perform the operation with the given name.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The URL lookup behavior is only done when the backing Context was
      created by the JNDI implementation in the JRE. If the backing Context
      had been created through the singleton provisioning mechanism, then no
      URL lookup is done for names that have a colon. The URL lookup
      responsibility is then left to the backing Context
      implementation.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3097699">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Object and Reference Conversion</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class provides a way to create
      objects from a <fo:inline font-style="italic">description</fo:inline> with the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method. In general, it will iterate over
      a number of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects and ask each one of them
      to provide the requested object. The first non-<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> result
      indicates success. These <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects are created
      from an environment property.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A special case for the description argument in the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method is the
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">Reference</fo:inline>. A Reference is a description of an
      object that can be stored persistently. It can be re-created into an
      actual object through the static <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method
      of the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class. The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline>
      object describes the actual <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> implementing
      class that must be used to create the object.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This default behavior is completely replaced with the Object
      Factory Builder singleton by getting the to be used
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> object directly from the set singleton Object
      Factory Builder.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3083484">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.5</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Environment</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">JNDI clients need a way to set the configuration properties to
      select the proper JNDI Provider. For example, a JNDI Provider might
      require an identity and a password in order to access the service. This
      type of configuration is referred to as the
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">environment</fo:inline> of a Context. The environment is a set
      of properties. Common property names can be found in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3109941">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[3] <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Standard Property Names</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The set of properties is build from the following
      sources (in priority order, that is later entries are shadowed by
      earlier entries):</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                              id="d95e410">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e411">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Properties set in the environment <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Hashtable</fo:inline>
          object given in the constructor argument (if any) of the
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e418">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Properties from the Java System Properties</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e420">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Properties found in
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">$JAVA_HOME/lib/jndi.properties</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">There are some special rules around the handling of specific
      properties.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3082552">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.6</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Naming Manager Singletons</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The default behavior of the JRE implementation of JNDI can be
      extended in a standardized way. The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class has
      two static singletons that allow JNDI Providers outside the JRE to
      provide <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> and
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects. These singletons are set with the
      following static methods on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e437">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e438">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">setObjectFactoryBuilder(ObjectFactoryBuilder)</fo:inline> - A
          hook to provide <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e444">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">setInitialContextFactoryBuilder(InitialContextFactoryBuilder)</fo:inline>
          - A hook to provide <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> objects. This
          hook is consulted to create a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object that will
          be associated with an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object the client
          creates.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">These JNDI Provider hooks are <fo:inline font-style="italic">singletons</fo:inline> and
      must be set <fo:inline font-style="italic">before</fo:inline> any application code creates an
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object or any objects are converted. If
      these singletons are not set, the JNDI implementation in the JRE will
      provide a default behavior that is based on searching through classes
      defined in an environment property.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Both singletons can only be set once. A second attempt to set
      these singletons results in an Illegal State Exception being
      thrown.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3094617">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.2.7</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Built-In JNDI Providers</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Java Runtime Environment (JRE) defines the following default
      providers:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e466">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e467">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">LDAP</fo:inline> - Lightweight Directory Access
          Protocol (LDAP) service provider</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e471">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">COS</fo:inline> - CORBA Object Service (COS) naming
          service provider</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e475">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">RMI</fo:inline> - Remote Method Invocation (RMI)
          Registry service provider</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e479">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">DNS</fo:inline> - Domain Name System (DNS) service
          provider</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Although these are the default JNDI Service Providers, the JNDI
      architecture provides a number of mechanisms to plug-in new types of
      providers.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d95e484">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">JNDI Context Manager Service</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.3</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>JNDI Context Manager Service</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Context Manager service allows clients to obtain a Context
    using the OSGi service model. By obtaining a JNDI Context Manager service,
    a client can get a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object so that it can interact
    with the available JNDI Providers. This service replaces the approach
    where the creation of a new <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object provided
    the client with access to an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object that was
    backed by a JNDI Provider's Context.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">JNDIContextManager</fo:inline> interface defines the following
    methods for obtaining <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d95e500">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e501">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIContextManager.newInitialContext--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">newInitialContext()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> - Obtain a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object using
        the default environment properties.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e507">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIContextManager.newInitialContext-Map-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">newInitialContext(Map)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> - Get a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object using the
        default environment properties merged with the given
        properties.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e513">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIContextManager.newInitialDirContext--">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">newInitialDirContext()</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> - Get a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">DirContext</fo:inline> object using a
        default environment properties.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e519">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIContextManager.newInitialDirContext-Map-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">newInitialDirContext(Map)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link> -Get a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">DirContext</fo:inline> object using
        the default environment properties merged with the given
        properties.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Context Manager service returns <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline>
    objects that implement the same behavior as the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class; the returned Context object does not
    actually extend the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class, its only guarantee
    is that it implements the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object is a facade for the context that is
    created by the JNDI Provider. This JNDI Provider's Context is called the
    <fo:inline font-style="italic">backing Context</fo:inline>. This is similar to the behavior of
    the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class. However, in this specification, the
    facade can change or loose the backing Context due to the dynamics of the
    OSGi framework.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The returned facade must also provides URL lookups, just like an
    Initial Context. However, the URL Context lookup must be based on Object
    Factory services with a service property that defines the scheme.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The environment properties used to create the backing Context are
    constructed in a similar way as the environment properties of the Java SE
    JNDI, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i3119408">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">Environment and Bundles</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3119408"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The following sections define in detail how a JNDI Provider Context
    must be created and managed.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3119408">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.3.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Environment and Bundles</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Java SE JNDI looks for a file in
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">$JAVAHOME/lib/jndi.properties</fo:inline>, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3083484">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Environment</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3083484"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. A JNDI Implementation must not use this
      information but it must use a resource in the bundle that uses the JNDI
      Context Manager service. The order is therefore:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                              id="d95e557">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e558">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Properties set in the environment <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Hashtable</fo:inline>
          object given in the constructor argument (if any) of the
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e565">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Properties from the Java System Properties</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e567">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>A properties resource from the bundle that uses the service
          called <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">/jndi.properties</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The following four properties do not overwrite other properties
      but are merged:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e573">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e574">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.object</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e577">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.state</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e580">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.control</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e583">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.url.pkgs</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">These property values are considered lists and the ultimate value
      used by the JNDI Providers is taken by merging the values found in each
      stage into a single colon separated list. For more information see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3109941">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">[3] <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Standard Property Names</fo:inline>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The environment consists of the merged properties. This
      environment is then passed to the Initial Context Factory Builder for
      the creation of an Initial Context Factory.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3092215">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.3.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Context Creation</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When a client calls one of the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">newInitialContext</fo:inline> (or
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">newInitialDirContext</fo:inline>) methods, the JNDI Context Manager
      service must construct an object that implements the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> interface based on the environment properties. All
      factory methods in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> and
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> classes take a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Hashtable</fo:inline> object with the environment as an argument, see
      <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3119408">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Environment and Bundles</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3119408"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The caller normally provides a specific property in the
      environment that specifies the class name of a provider class. This
      property is named:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e611">java.naming.factory.initial</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The algorithm to find the provider of the requested Context can
      differ depending on the presence or absence of the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.initial</fo:inline> property in the
      environment.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">In the following sections the cases for presence or absence of the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.initial</fo:inline> property are described. Several
      steps in these algorithm iterate over a set of available services. This
      iteration must always take place in ranking order as specified in
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference.compareTo</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Exception handling in the following steps is as follows:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e623">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e624">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>If an Exception is thrown by an Initial Context Factory
          Builder service, then this Exception must be logged but further
          ignored.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e626">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Exceptions thrown by the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline>
          objects when creating a Context must be thrown to the caller.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block id="i3093402">
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                                  margin-left="0pt"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                              <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                        xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                        font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-weight="normal"
                                        keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                        space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        start-indent="0pt"
                                        hyphenate="false">
                                 <fo:block font-size="9pt"
                                           line-height="11pt"
                                           space-before="5pt"
                                           space-after="5pt">
                                    <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                   provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                       <fo:list-item>
                                          <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                             <fo:block>126.3.2.1</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-label>
                                          <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                             <fo:block>Implementation Class Present in Environment</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-body>
                                       </fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                 </fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt">If the implementation class is specified, a JNDI Provider is
        searched in the service registry with the following steps, which stop
        when a backing Context can be created:</fo:block>
                  <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                                 space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                 space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                 space-after.optimum="1em"
                                 space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                                 space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                 provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                                 id="d95e634">
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e635">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>Find a service in ranking order that has a name matching the
            given implementation class name as well as the
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> class name. The searching must
            take place through the Bundle Context of the requesting bundle but
            must not require that the requesting bundle imports the package of
            the implementation class. If such a matching Initial Context
            Factory service is found, it must be used to construct the
            <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                            font-size="9pt"
                                            letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object that will act as the backing
            Context.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e642">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>Get all the Initial Context Factory Builder services. For
            each such service, in ranking order:</fo:block>
                              <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                             provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                             id="d95e644">
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d95e645">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>Ask the Initial Context Factory Builder service to
                create a new <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> object. If
                this is <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> then continue with the next
                service.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d95e652">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>Create the Context with the found Initial Context
                Factory and return it.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e654">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>If no backing Context could be found using these steps, then
            the JNDI Context Manager service must throw a No Initial Context
            Exception.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block id="i3121179">
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                                  margin-left="0pt"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                           <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                              <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                        xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                        font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-weight="normal"
                                        keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                        space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        start-indent="0pt"
                                        hyphenate="false">
                                 <fo:block font-size="9pt"
                                           line-height="11pt"
                                           space-before="5pt"
                                           space-after="5pt">
                                    <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                   provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                       <fo:list-item>
                                          <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                             <fo:block>126.3.2.2</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-label>
                                          <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                             <fo:block>No Implementation Class Specified</fo:block>
                                          </fo:list-item-body>
                                       </fo:list-item>
                                    </fo:list-block>
                                 </fo:block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
                  <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                            space-before.minimum="5pt"
                            space-before.maximum="5pt">If the environment does not contain a value for the
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                font-size="9pt"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.initial</fo:inline> property then the following
        steps must be used to find a backing <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                font-size="9pt"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline>
        object.</fo:block>
                  <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                                 space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                 space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                 space-after.optimum="1em"
                                 space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                                 space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                                 provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                 provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                                 id="d95e664">
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e665">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>Get all the Initial Context Factory Builder services. For
            each such service, in ranking order, do:</fo:block>
                              <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                             provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                             id="d95e667">
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d95e668">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>Ask the Initial Context Factory Builder service to
                create a new <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> object. If
                this is <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>, then continue with the next
                service.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d95e675">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>Create the backing <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object with the
                found Initial Context Factory service and return it.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e680">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>Get all the Initial Context Factory services. For each such
            service, in ranking order, do:</fo:block>
                              <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                             provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                             id="d95e682">
                                 <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                               space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                               id="d95e683">
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                       <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>
                                          <fo:block>Ask the Initial Context Factory service to create a new
                <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object. If this is <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                        font-size="9pt"
                                                        letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> then
                continue with the next service otherwise create a new Context
                with the created Context as the backing Context.</fo:block>
                                       </fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                     <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                   space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                   id="d95e690">
                        <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                           <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-label>
                        <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:block>If no Context has been found, an initial Context is returned
            without any backing. This returned initial Context can then only
            be used to perform URL based lookups.</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:list-item-body>
                     </fo:list-item>
                  </fo:list-block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e693">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.3.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Rebinding</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI Provider can be added or removed to the service registry at
      any time because it is an OSGi service; OSGi services are by their
      nature dynamic. When a JNDI Provider unregisters an Initial Context
      Factory that was used to create a backing service then the JNDI Context
      Manager service must remove the association between any returned
      Contexts and their now invalid backing Contexts.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Context Manager service must try to find a replacement
      whenever it is accessed and no backing Context is available. However, if
      no such replacement can be found the called function must result in
      throwing a No Initial Context Exception.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e697">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.3.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Life Cycle and Dynamism</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When a client has finished with a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object,
      then the client must close this <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object by calling
      the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">close</fo:inline> method. When a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object is
      closed, the resources held by the JNDI Implementation on the client's
      behalf for that Context must all be released. Releasing these resources
      must not affect other, independent, <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects
      returned to the same client.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If a client ungets the JNDI Context Manager service, all the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects returned through that service instance must
      automatically be closed by the JNDI Context Manager. When the JNDI
      Context Manager service is unregistered, the JNDI Context Manager must
      automatically close all Contexts held.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">For more information about life cycle issues, see also <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3079918">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Life Cycle Mismatch</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3079918"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i3093106">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">JNDI Provider Admin service</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.4</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>JNDI Provider Admin service</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">JNDI provides a general object conversion service, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i3097699">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object and Reference Conversion</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3097699"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. For this specification, the responsibility of the
    static method on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline>
               <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> is replaced with the JNDI Provider Admin
    service. The <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">JNDIProviderAdmin</fo:inline> interface provides the
    following methods that can be used to convert a description object to an
    object:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d95e731">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e732">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIProviderAdmin.getObjectInstance-Object-javax.naming.Name-javax.naming.Context-Map-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getObjectInstance(Object,Name,Context,Map)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
        - Used by Context implementations to convert a description object to
        another object.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e737">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIProviderAdmin.getObjectInstance-Object-javax.naming.Name-javax.naming.Context-Map-javax.naming.directory.Attributes-">
                              <fo:inline color="blue"
                                         font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                         hyphenate="false">getObjectInstance(Object,Name,Context,Map,Attributes)</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>
        - Used by a Dir Context implementations to convert a description
        object to another object.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">In either case, the first argument is an object, called the
    <fo:inline font-style="italic">description</fo:inline>. JNDI allows a number of different Java
    types here. When either method is called, the following algorithm is
    followed to find a matching Object Factory to find/create the requested
    object. This algorithm is identical for both methods, except that the call
    that takes the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Attributes</fo:inline> argument consults Dir Object
    Factory services first and then Object Factory services while the method
    without the Attributes parameter only consults Object Factory
    services.</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                           id="d95e748">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e749">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If the description object is an instance of
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Referenceable</fo:inline>, then get the corresponding
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> object and use this as the description
        object.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e756">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If the description object is not a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> object
        then goto step <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="i3112833">
                              <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                         font-family="inherit"
                                         letter-spacing="inherit"
                                         hyphenate="inherit">5</fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e763">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If a factory class name is specified, the JNDI Provider Admin
        service uses its own Bundle Context to search for a service registered
        under the Reference's factory class name. If a matching Object Factory
        is found then it is used to create the object from the
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> object and the algorithm stops here.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="i3112861">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>4.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If no factory class name is specified, iterate over all the
        Reference object's <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">StringRefAddrs</fo:inline> objects with the
        address type of <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">URL</fo:inline>. For each matching address type, use
        the value to find a matching URL Context, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                          xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                          internal-destination="i3116133">
                              <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                         font-family="inherit"
                                         letter-spacing="inherit"
                                         hyphenate="inherit">
                                 <fo:inline font-style="italic">URL Context Provider</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3116133"/>
                              </fo:inline>
                           </fo:basic-link>, and use it to recreate the object. See the
        Naming Manager for details. If an object is created then it is
        returned and the algorithm stops here.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="i3112833">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>5.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>Iterate over the Object Factory Builder services in ranking
        order. Attempt to use each such service to create an
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">DirObjectFactory</fo:inline> instance.
        If this succeeds (non <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>) then use this
        <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">DirObjectFactory</fo:inline> instance
        to recreate the object. If successful, the algorithm stops
        here.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e790">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>6.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If the description was a Reference and without a factory class
        name specified, or if the description was not of type Reference, then
        attempt to convert the object with each Object Factory service (or Dir
        Object Factory service for directories) service in ranking order until
        a non-<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline> value is returned.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e795">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>7.</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>If no <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> implementations can be located
        to resolve the given description object, the description object is
        returned.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">If an Exception occurs during the use of an Object Factory Builder
    service then this exception should be logged but must be ignored. If,
    however, an Exception occurs during the calling of a found
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">DirObjecFactory</fo:inline> object then
    this Exception must be re-thrown to the caller of the JNDI Provider Admin
    service.</fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d95e806">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">JNDI Providers</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.5</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>JNDI Providers</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">JNDI Providers can be registered by registering an appropriate
    service. These services are consulted by the JNDI Implementation for
    creating a Context as well as creating/finding/converting general
    objects.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e809">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Initial Context Factory Builder Provider</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Initial Context Factory Builder provider is asked to provide an
      Initial Context Factory when no implementation class is specified or no
      such implementation can be found. An Initial Context Factory Builder
      service can be used by containers for other bundles to control the
      initial Context their applications receive.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Initial Context Factory Builder provider must register an
      Initial Context Factory Builder service. The iteration ordering of
      multiple Initial Context Factory Builder services must always take place
      in ranking order as specified in
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference.compareTo</fo:inline>. Implementations must be careful
      to correctly provide defaults.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">For example, a container could use a thread local variable to mark
      the stack for a specific application. The implementation of the Initial
      Context Factory Builder can then detect specific calls from this
      application. To make the next code example work, an instance must be
      registered as an Initial Context Factory Builder service.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e817">public class Container implements InitialContextFactoryBuilder {
    ThreadLocal&lt;Application&gt; apps;

    void startApp(final Application app) {
        Thread appThread = new Thread(app.getName()) {
            public void run() {
                apps.set(app);
                    app.run();
    }}}

    public InitialContextFactory 
        createInitialContextFactory( Hashtable&lt;?,?&gt; ht ) {
        final Application app = apps.get();
        if ( app == null )
          return null;

        return new InitialContextFactory() {
            public Context getInitialContext( Hashtable&lt;?,?&gt;env) {
                return app.getContext(env);
            }
        };
 } }</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e818">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Initial Context Factory Provider</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Initial Context Factory provides Contexts of a specific type.
      For example, those contexts allow communications with an LDAP server. An
      Initial Context Factory Provider must register the its Initial Context
      Factory service under the following names:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e821">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e822">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Implementation Class</fo:inline> - An Initial Context
          Factory provider must register a service under the name of the
          implementation class. This allows the JNDI Context Manager to find
          implementations specified in the environment properties.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e826">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Initial Context Factory</fo:inline> - As a general
          Initial Context Factory. If registered as such, it can be consulted
          for a default Initial Context. Implementations must be careful to
          only return a Context when the environment properties are
          appropriate. See <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                             xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                             internal-destination="i3121179">
                                 <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                            font-family="inherit"
                                            letter-spacing="inherit"
                                            hyphenate="inherit">
                                    <fo:inline font-style="italic">No Implementation Class Specified</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3121179"/>
                                 </fo:inline>
                              </fo:basic-link>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Initial Context Factory service can create both
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">DirContext</fo:inline> as well as <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> objects.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">For example, SUN JREs for Java SE provide an implementation of a
      Context that can answer DNS questions. The name of the implementation
      class is a well known constant. The following class can be used with
      Declarative Services to provide a lazy implementation of a DNS
      Context:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e838">public class DNSProvider implements InitialContextFactory{
    public Context createInitialContextFactory( Hashtable&lt;?,?&gt;env ) throws 
        NamingException {
        try {
            Class&lt;InitialContextFactory&gt; cf = (Class&lt;InitialContextFactory&gt;)
                l.loadClass("com.sun.jndi.dns.DnsContextFactory" );
            InitialContextFactory icf = cf.newInstance();
            return icf.createInitialContextFactory(env);
        } catch( Throwable t ) {
            return null;
        }
    }
}</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e839">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Object Factory Builder Provider</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Object Factory Builder provider must register an Object Factory
      Builder service. Such a service can be used to provide
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> and/or <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">DirObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects.
      An Object Factory Builder service is requested for such an object when
      no specific converter can be found. This service can be leveraged by
      bundles that act as a container for other bundles to control the object
      conversion for their subjects.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e847">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Object Factory Provider</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">An Object Factory provider can participate in the conversion of
      objects. It must register a service under the following names:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e850">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e851">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Implementation Class</fo:inline> - A service
          registered under its implementation class can be leveraged by a
          description that is a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> object. Such an object
          can contain the name of the factory class. The implementation class
          can implement the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">DirObjectFactory</fo:inline> interface or the
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> interface.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e861">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object Factory</fo:inline> - The
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> interface is necessary to ensure class
          space consistency.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e867">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Dir Object Factory</fo:inline> - If the Object
          Factory provider can accept the additional Attributes argument in
          the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method of the JNDI Provider Admin
          service than it must also register as a Dir Object Factory
          service.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3116133">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.5</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>URL Context Provider</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A <fo:inline font-style="italic">URL Context Factory</fo:inline> is a special type of an
      Object Factory service. A URL Context Factory must be registered as an
      Object Factory service with the following service property:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e879">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e880">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi.jndi.url.scheme</fo:inline> - The URL scheme associated
          with this URL Context, for example <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">acme</fo:inline>. The scheme
          must not contain the colon (<fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">':' \u003A</fo:inline>).</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A URL Context is used for URL based operations on an initial
      Context. For example, a lookup to
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">acme:foo/javax.sql.DataSource</fo:inline> must not use the provider
      based lookup mechanism of the backing Context but instead causes a
      lookup for the requested URL Context. A URL Context also provides a
      secondary mechanism for restoring <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> objects.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When an initial Context returned by the JNDI Context Manager
      service is given a URL based operation, it searches in the service
      registry for an Object Factory service that is published with the URL
      scheme property that matches the scheme used from the lookup
      request.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">It then calls the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getInstance</fo:inline> method on the Object
      Factory service with the following parameters:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                              id="d95e899">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e900">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object</fo:inline> - Should be either a
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String</fo:inline>, <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">String[]</fo:inline>, or
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e910">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Name</fo:inline> - must be <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e915">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Context</fo:inline> - must be
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e920">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>
                              <fo:inline font-style="italic">Hashtable</fo:inline> - The environment
          properties.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Calling the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getInstance</fo:inline> method must return a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object. This context is then used to perform the
      lookup.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The life cycle of the Object Factory used to create the URL
      Context is tied to the JNDI context that was used to perform the URL
      based JNDI operation. By the time JNDI context is closed any
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> objects held to process the URL lookups must
      be released (unget).</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3104232">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.5.6</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>JRE Context Providers</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The Java Runtime Environment (JRE) defines a number of default
      naming providers., see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3094617">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Built-In JNDI Providers</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3094617"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. These naming
      providers are not OSGi aware, but are commonly used and are provided by
      the JRE. These naming providers rely on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline>
      class for object conversion and finding URL Contexts.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JRE default providers are made available by the JNDI
      Implementation. This JNDI Implementation must register a
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">built-in</fo:inline> Initial Context Factory Builder service
      that is capable of loading any <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline>
      classes of the JRE providers.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">When this built-in Initial Context Factory Builder is called to
      create an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> object it must look in the
      environment properties that were given as an argument and extract the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">java.naming.factory.initial</fo:inline> property; this property
      contains the name of the class of a provider. The built-in Initial
      Context Factory Builder then must use the bootstrap class loader to load
      the given <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactory</fo:inline> class and creates a new
      instance with the no arguments constructor and return it. If this fails,
      it must return <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">null</fo:inline>. This mechanism will allow loading of
      any built-in providers.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This built-in Initial Context Factory Builder service must be
      registered with no <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">service.ranking</fo:inline> property. This will give
      it the default ranking and allows other providers to override the
      default.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="i3134320">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">OSGi URL Scheme</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.6</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>OSGi URL Scheme</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A URL scheme is available that allows JNDI based applications to
    access services in the service registry, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i3113878">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">Services and State</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3113878"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>
    about restrictions on these services. The URL scheme is specified as
    follows:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e968">service   ::= 'osgi:service/' query
query     ::= jndi-name |  qname ( '/' filter )?
jndi-name ::= &lt;any string&gt;</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">No spaces are allowed between the terms.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This OSGi URL scheme can be used to perform a lookup of a single
    matching service using the interface name and filter. The URL Context must
    use the <fo:inline font-style="italic">owning bundle</fo:inline> to perform the service queries.
    The owning bundle is the bundle that requested the initial Context from
    the JNDI Context Manager service or received its Context through the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class. The returned objects must not be
    incompatible with the class space of the owning bundle.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">The lookup for a URL with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:</fo:inline> scheme and
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">service</fo:inline> path returns the service whose
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference</fo:inline> is first in ranking order as specified in
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">ServiceReference.compareTo</fo:inline>. This scheme only allows a single
    service to be found. Multiple services can be obtained with the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:</fo:inline> scheme and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">servicelist</fo:inline> path:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e991">servicelist ::= 'osgi:servicelist/' query?</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">If this <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:servicelist</fo:inline> scheme is used from a lookup
    method then a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> object is returned instead of a service
    object. Calling the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">listBindings</fo:inline> method will produce a
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingEnumeration</fo:inline> object that provides <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Binding</fo:inline>
    objects. A Binding object contains the name, class of the service, and the
    service object. The bound object is the service object contained in the
    given Context.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">When the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> class <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">list</fo:inline> method is
    called, the Naming Enumeration object provides a
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NameClassPair</fo:inline> object. This <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NameClassPair</fo:inline> object
    will include the name and class of each service in the Context. The
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">list</fo:inline> method can be useful in cases where a client wishes to
    iterate over the available services without actually getting them. If the
    service itself is required, then <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">listBindings</fo:inline> method should
    be used.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">If multiple services matched the criteria listed in the URL, there
    would be more than one service available in the Context, and the
    corresponding Naming Enumeration would contain the same number of
    services.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">If multiple services match, a call to <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">listBindings</fo:inline> on
    this Context would return a list of bindings whose name are a string with
    the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">service.id</fo:inline> number, for example:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e1027">1283</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Thus the following lookup is valid:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e1029">osgi:servicelist/javax.sql.DataSource/(&amp;(db=mydb)(version=3.1))</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A service can provide a <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI service name</fo:inline> if it
    provides the following service property:</fo:block>
            <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                           space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                           space-after.optimum="1em"
                           space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                           space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                           provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                           provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                           id="d95e1034">
               <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                             space-before.minimum="2pt"
                             space-before.maximum="2pt"
                             id="d95e1035">
                  <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                     <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-label>
                  <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                     <fo:block>
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi.jndi.service.name</fo:inline> - An alternative name that
        the service can be looked up by when the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                      font-size="9pt"
                                      letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:</fo:inline> URL scheme
        is used.</fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:list-item-body>
               </fo:list-item>
            </fo:list-block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">If a service is published with a JNDI service name then the service
    matches any URL that has this service name in the place of
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">interface</fo:inline>. For example, if the JNDI service name is
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">foo</fo:inline>, then the following URL selects this service:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e1047">osgi:service/foo</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">Using a JNDI service name that can be interpreted as an interface
    name must be avoided, if this happens the result is undefined.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI client can also obtain the Bundle Context of the owning
    bundle by using the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:</fo:inline> scheme namespace with the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">framework/bundleContext</fo:inline> name. The following URL must return
    the Bundle Context of the owning bundle:</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-before.optimum="1em"
                      space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                      space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                      space-after.optimum="1em"
                      space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                      hyphenate="false"
                      wrap-option="no-wrap"
                      white-space-collapse="false"
                      white-space-treatment="preserve"
                      linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                      text-align="start"
                      font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                      font-size="9pt"
                      letter-spacing="-.0em"
                      space-before="5pt"
                      space-after="3pt"
                      space-after.conditionality="retain"
                      start-indent="inherit"
                      line-height="11pt"
                      id="d95e1055">osgi:framework/bundleContext</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">After the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingEnumeration</fo:inline> object has been used it
    must be closed by the client. Implementations must then unget any gotten
    services or perform other cleanup.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1061">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.6.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Service Proxies</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The OSGi URL Context handles the complexities by hiding the
      dynamic nature of OSGi. The OSGi URL Context must handle the dynamics by
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">proxying</fo:inline> the service objects. This proxy must
      implement the interface given in the URL. If the JNDI service name
      instead of a class name is used, then all interfaces under which the
      service is registered must be implemented. If an interface is not
      compatible with the owning bundle's class space then it must not be
      implemented on the proxy, it must then be ignored. If this results in no
      implemented interfaces then an Illegal Argument Exception must be
      thrown.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Interfaces can always be proxied but classes are much harder. For
      this reason, an implementation is free to throw an Illegal Argument
      Exception when a class is used in the URL or in one of the registration
      names.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Getting the actual service object can be delayed until the proxy
      is actually used to call a method. If a method is called and the actual
      service has been unregistered, then the OSGi URL Context must attempt to
      rebind it to another service that matches the criteria given in the URL
      the next time it is called. When no alternative service is available, a
      Service Exception with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">UNREGISTERED</fo:inline> type code must be
      thrown. Services obtained with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:</fo:inline> URL scheme must
      therefore be stateless because the rebinding to alternative services is
      not visible to the caller; there are no listeners defined for this
      rebinding, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3113878">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Services and State</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3113878"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">If the reference was looked up using <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi:servicelist</fo:inline>
      then proxies must still be used, however, these proxies must not rebind
      when their underlying service is unregistered. Instead, they must throw
      a Service Exception with the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">UNREGISTERED</fo:inline> type whenever the
      proxy is used and the proxied service is no longer available.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3113878">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.6.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Services and State</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A service obtained through a URL Context lookup is proxied. During
      the usage of this service, the JNDI Implementation can be forced to
      transparently rebind this service to another instance. The JNDI
      specification is largely intended for portability. For this reason, it
      has no mechanism architected to receive notifications about this
      rebinding. The client code is therefore unable to handle the
      dynamics.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The consequence of this model is that stateful services require
      extra care because applications cannot rely on the fact that they always
      communicate with the same service. Virtually all OSGi specified services
      have state.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d95e1086">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Traditional Client Model</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.7</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Traditional Client Model</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI Implementation must at startup register the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> object and the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> object with the
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class. As described in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i3095960">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Overview</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3095960"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>, the JNDI code in the JRE will then delegate all
    Context related requests to the JNDI Implementation. Setting these
    singletons allows code that is not aware of the OSGi framework to use
    <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                          font-size="9pt"
                          letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> implementations from JNDI Providers registered with
    the OSGi service registry and that are managed as bundles. The JNDI
    Implementation therefore acts as a broker to the service registry for OSGi
    unaware code.</fo:block>
            <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                      space-before.minimum="5pt"
                      space-before.maximum="5pt">This brokering role can only be played when the JNDI Implementation
    can set the singletons as specified in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                              xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                              internal-destination="i3082552">
                  <fo:inline color="inherit"
                             font-family="inherit"
                             letter-spacing="inherit"
                             hyphenate="inherit">
                     <fo:inline font-style="italic">Naming Manager Singletons</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3082552"/>
                  </fo:inline>
               </fo:basic-link>. If the
    JNDI Implementation cannot set these singletons then it should log an
    error with the Log Service, if available. It can then not perform the
    following sections.</fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1104">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.7.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>New Initial Context</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The client typically requests a Context using the following
      code:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e1107">Hashtable env = new Hashtable();
env.put(Context.INITIAL_CONTEXT_FACTORY, "com.sun.jndi.ldap.LdapCtxFactory");
InitialContext ctx = new InitialContext(env);</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The created <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object is a facade for the
      real Context that is requested by the caller. It provides the
      bootstrapping mechanism for JNDI Provider plugability. In order to
      obtain the provider's Context, the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class
      makes a call to the static <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getContext</fo:inline> method on the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class. The JNDI code in the JRE then
      delegates any request for an initial Context object to the JNDI
      Implementation through the registered
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> singleton. The JNDI
      Implementation then determines the Bundle Context of the caller as
      described in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3081937">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Caller's Bundle Context</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3081937"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. If no such Bundle Context can
      be found, a No Initial Context Exception is thrown to the caller. This
      Bundle Context must be from an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ACTIVE</fo:inline> bundle.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">This Bundle Context is then used to get the JNDI Context Manager
      service. This service is then used as described in <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3092215">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Context Creation</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3092215"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> to get an initial Context. This initial Context is
      then used in the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object as the
      <fo:inline font-style="italic">default initial context</fo:inline>. In this specification this
      is normally called the backing context. An <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline>
      object constructed through an Initial Context Factory Builder will not
      use the URL lookup mechanism, it must delegate all operations to the its
      backing context. A Context obtained through the JNDI Context Manager
      provides the URL lookup behavior instead.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1135">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.7.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Static Conversion</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">JNDI provides a general object conversion facility that is used by
      the URL Context and the process of restoring an object from a
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Reference</fo:inline> object, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3097699">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Object and Reference Conversion</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3097699"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. A JNDI
      Implementation must take over this conversion by setting the static
      Object Factory Builder singleton, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3082552">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Naming Manager Singletons</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3082552"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>.
      Non-OSGi aware <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">Context</fo:inline> implementations will use the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> static <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method
      for object conversion. This method then delegates to the set singleton
      Object Factory Builder to obtain an <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactory</fo:inline> object
      that understands how to convert the given description to an object. The
      JNDI Implementation must return an Object Factory that understands the
      OSGi service registry. If the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline> method is
      called on this object it must use the same rules as defined for the JNDI
      Provider Admin service <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="org.osgi.service.jndi.JNDIProviderAdmin.getObjectInstance-Object-javax.naming.Name-javax.naming.Context-Map-">
                     <fo:inline color="blue"
                                font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                letter-spacing="0.08em"
                                hyphenate="false">getObjectInstance(Object,javax.naming.Name,javax.naming.Context,Map)</fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link> method, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3093106">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">JNDI Provider Admin service</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3093106"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The
      Bundle Context that must be used with respect to this service is the
      caller's Bundle Context, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3081937">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Caller's Bundle Context</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3081937"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. If the Bundle
      Context is not found, the description object must be returned. The
      calling bundle must not be required to import the
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">org.osgi.service.jndi</fo:inline> package.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3081937">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.7.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Caller's Bundle Context</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The following mechanisms are used to determine the callers Bundle
      Context:</fo:block>
               <fo:list-block space-before.optimum="1em"
                              space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                              space-after.optimum="1em"
                              space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                              space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                              provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                              provisional-distance-between-starts="14pt"
                              id="d95e1168">
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e1169">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>1.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Look in the JNDI environment properties for a property
          called</fo:block>
                           <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                     space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                     space-before.maximum="5pt">
                              <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-before.optimum="1em"
                                        space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                        space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                                        space-after.optimum="1em"
                                        space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                                        hyphenate="false"
                                        wrap-option="no-wrap"
                                        white-space-collapse="false"
                                        white-space-treatment="preserve"
                                        linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                                        text-align="start"
                                        font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                        font-size="9pt"
                                        letter-spacing="-.0em"
                                        space-before="5pt"
                                        space-after="3pt"
                                        space-after.conditionality="retain"
                                        start-indent="inherit"
                                        line-height="11pt"
                                        id="d95e1172">osgi.service.jndi.bundleContext</fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                           <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                                     space-before.minimum="5pt"
                                     space-before.maximum="5pt">If a value for this property exists then use it as the Bundle
          Context. If the Bundle Context has been found stop.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e1174">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>2.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Obtain the Thread Context Class Loader; if it, or an ancestor
          class loader, implements the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">BundleReference</fo:inline> interface,
          call its <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getBundle</fo:inline> method to get the client's Bundle;
          then call <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getBundleContext</fo:inline> on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">Bundle</fo:inline>
          object to get the client's Bundle Context. If the Bundle Context has
          been found stop.</fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
                  <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                id="d95e1185">
                     <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                        <fo:block>3.</fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-label>
                     <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                        <fo:block>
                           <fo:block>Walk the call stack until the invoker is found. The invoker
          can be the caller of the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class
          constructor or the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> or
          <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">DirectoryManager</fo:inline>
                              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                         font-size="9pt"
                                         letter-spacing="0.08em">getObjectInstance</fo:inline>
          methods.</fo:block>
                           <fo:list-block provisional-label-separation="0.2em"
                                          provisional-distance-between-starts="12pt"
                                          id="d95e1196">
                              <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                            id="d95e1197">
                                 <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                    <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-label>
                                 <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                    <fo:block>
                                       <fo:block>Get the class loader of the caller and see if it, or an
              ancestor, implements the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                     font-size="9pt"
                                                     letter-spacing="0.08em">BundleReference</fo:inline>
              interface.</fo:block>
                                    </fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-body>
                              </fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                            id="d95e1202">
                                 <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                    <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-label>
                                 <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                    <fo:block>
                                       <fo:block>If a Class Loader implementing the
              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                     font-size="9pt"
                                                     letter-spacing="0.08em">BundleReference</fo:inline> interface is found call the
              <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                     font-size="9pt"
                                                     letter-spacing="0.08em">getBundle</fo:inline> method to get the clients Bundle; then
              call the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                                     font-size="9pt"
                                                     letter-spacing="0.08em">getBundleContext</fo:inline> method on the Bundle to
              get the clients Bundle Context.</fo:block>
                                    </fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-body>
                              </fo:list-item>
                              <fo:list-item space-before.optimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.minimum="2pt"
                                            space-before.maximum="2pt"
                                            id="d95e1211">
                                 <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()">
                                    <fo:block>•</fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-label>
                                 <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                    <fo:block>
                                       <fo:block>If the Bundle Context has been found stop, else continue
              with the next stack frame.</fo:block>
                                    </fo:block>
                                 </fo:list-item-body>
                              </fo:list-item>
                           </fo:list-block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:list-item-body>
                  </fo:list-item>
               </fo:list-block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="i3079918">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.7.4</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>Life Cycle Mismatch</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The use of static access to the JNDI mechanisms,
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> and <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> class
      methods, in the traditional client programming model produces several
      problems with regard to the OSGi life cycle. The primary problem being
      that there is no dependency management in place when static methods are
      used. These problems do not exist for the JNDI Context Manager service.
      Therefore, OSGi applications are strongly encouraged to use the JNDI
      Context Manager service.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The traditional programming model approach relies on two JVM
      singletons in the Naming Manager, see <fo:basic-link xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                 xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                 internal-destination="i3082552">
                     <fo:inline color="inherit"
                                font-family="inherit"
                                letter-spacing="inherit"
                                hyphenate="inherit">
                        <fo:inline font-style="italic">Naming Manager Singletons</fo:inline> on page <fo:page-number-citation ref-id="i3082552"/>
                     </fo:inline>
                  </fo:basic-link>. The
      JNDI Implementation bundle must set both singletons before it registers
      its JNDI Context Manager service and JNDI Provider Admin service.
      However, in OSGi there is no defined start ordering, primarily because
      bundles can be updated at any moment in time and will at such time not
      be available to provide their function anyway. For this reason, OSGi
      bundles express their dependencies with services.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The lack of start ordering means that a bundle could create an
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContext</fo:inline> object before the JNDI Implementation has
      had the chance to set the static Initial Context Factory Builder
      singleton. This means that the JNDI implementation inside the JRE will
      provide its default behavior and likely have to throw an exception. A
      similar exception is thrown for the Object Factory Builder
      singleton.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">There is a also a (small) possibility that a client will call
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">new InitialContext()</fo:inline> after the singletons have been set,
      but before the JNDI Context Manager and JNDI Provider Admin services
      have been registered. This specification requires that these services
      are set after the singletons are set. In this race condition the JNDI
      Implementation should throw a No Initial Context Exception, explaining
      that the JNDI services are not available yet.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="d95e1233">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                  space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                  space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                  space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                  text-align="start"
                                  start-indent="0pt"
                                  hyphenate="false">
                           <fo:marker marker-class-name="section.head.marker">Security</fo:marker>
                           <fo:block font-size="18pt"
                                     line-height="25pt"
                                     space-before="12.5pt"
                                     space-after="12pt">
                              <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                             provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                 <fo:list-item>
                                    <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                       <fo:block>126.8</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-label>
                                    <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                       <fo:block>Security</fo:block>
                                    </fo:list-item-body>
                                 </fo:list-item>
                              </fo:list-block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1235">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.8.1</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>JNDI Implementation</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI Implementation may wish to assert that the user of the
      provider has some relevant Java 2 security permission. Since the JNDI
      implementation is an intermediary between the JNDI client and provider
      this means that the JNDI implementation needs to have any permissions
      required to access any JNDI Provider. As a result the JNDI
      implementation needs All Permission. This will result in the JNDI
      clients permissions being checked to see if it has the relevant
      permission to access the JNDI Provider.</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Implementation must make any invocation to access these
      services in a <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">doPriviledged</fo:inline> check. A JNDI client must
      therefore not be required to have the following permissions, which are
      needed by a JNDI Implementation:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e1242">ServicePermission ..ObjectFactory                REGISTER,GET
ServicePermission ..DirObjectFactory             REGISTER,GET
ServicePermission ..ObjectFactoryBuilder         REGISTER,GET
ServicePermission ..InitialContextFactory        REGISTER,GET
ServicePermission ..InitialContextFactoryBuilder REGISTER,GET
ServicePermission ..JNDIProviderAdmin            REGISTER,GET</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">The JNDI Implementation bundle must have the appropriate
      permissions to install the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">InitialContextFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> and
      <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">ObjectFactoryBuilder</fo:inline> instances using the appropriate
      methods on the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">NamingManager</fo:inline> class. This requires the
      following permission:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e1251">RuntimePermission "setFactory"</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1252">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.8.2</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>JNDI Clients</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI client using the JNDI Context Manager service must have the
      following permissions:</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-before.optimum="1em"
                         space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                         space-after.minimum="0.8em"
                         space-after.optimum="1em"
                         space-after.maximum="1.2em"
                         hyphenate="false"
                         wrap-option="no-wrap"
                         white-space-collapse="false"
                         white-space-treatment="preserve"
                         linefeed-treatment="preserve"
                         text-align="start"
                         font-family="ProductusOSGiMonoc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                         font-size="9pt"
                         letter-spacing="-.0em"
                         space-before="5pt"
                         space-after="3pt"
                         space-after.conditionality="retain"
                         start-indent="inherit"
                         line-height="11pt"
                         id="d95e1255">ServicePermission ..JNDIContextManager           GET</fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">Obtaining a reference to a JNDI Context Manager service should be
      considered a privileged operation and should be guarded by
      permissions.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
            <fo:block id="d95e1257">
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block>
                     <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                               margin-left="0pt"
                               font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                        <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                           <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                     xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                     font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                     font-weight="normal"
                                     keep-with-next.within-column="always"
                                     space-before.minimum="0.8em"
                                     space-before.optimum="1.0em"
                                     space-before.maximum="1.2em"
                                     text-align="start"
                                     start-indent="0pt"
                                     hyphenate="false">
                              <fo:block font-size="12pt"
                                        line-height="14pt"
                                        space-before="8pt"
                                        space-after="5pt">
                                 <fo:list-block provisional-distance-between-starts="1in"
                                                provisional-label-separation="0.090in">
                                    <fo:list-item>
                                       <fo:list-item-label end-indent="label-end()" text-align="start">
                                          <fo:block>126.8.3</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-label>
                                       <fo:list-item-body start-indent="body-start()">
                                          <fo:block>OSGi URL namespace</fo:block>
                                       </fo:list-item-body>
                                    </fo:list-item>
                                 </fo:list-block>
                              </fo:block>
                           </fo:block>
                        </fo:block>
                     </fo:block>
                  </fo:block>
               </fo:block>
               <fo:block space-before.optimum="5pt"
                         space-before.minimum="5pt"
                         space-before.maximum="5pt">A JNDI client must not be able to obtain services or a Bundle
      Context that the client bundle would not be able to get via the core
      OSGi API. To allow a client to use the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi</fo:inline> namespace to
      get a service the bundle must have the corresponding Service Permission.
      When using the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi</fo:inline> namespace to obtain the Bundle Context
      the client bundle must have Admin Permission for the Bundle Context.
      These permissions must be enforced by the <fo:inline font-family="ProductusOSGiBookc,ArialUnicodeMS"
                             font-size="9pt"
                             letter-spacing="0.08em">osgi</fo:inline> URL
      namespace handler. If there is no proper permission, the implementation
      must throw a Name Not Found Exception to prevent exposing the existence
      of such services.</fo:block>
            </fo:block>
         </fo:block>
         <fo:block id="org.osgi.service.jndi">
            <fo:block>
               <fo:block>
                  <fo:block keep-together.within-column="always"
                            margin-left="0pt"
                            font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS">
                     <fo:block keep-with-next.within-column="always">
                        <fo:block xmlns:d="http://docbook.org/ns/docbook"
                                  xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink"
                                  font-family="ProductusSemibold,ArialUnicodeMS"
                                  font-weight="normal"
                                  keep-with-next.within-column="always"
